{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791596305,"nonce":"Y/4a+AufJMsMKbnlLn8IuBqFLCM=","title":"CSS paint declarations as typed writes","message":"The cascade applied layout declarations natively and handed every paint declaration to the host as text, so each host parsed colours, gradients and the rest itself, and one of them read nine properties and dropped the rest. paint_writes (css/paint.rs) is the paint counterpart of layout_writes: it reads one declaration, or its unset, into typed writes built from blinc_core types, and None for a property that is not paint.\n\nReads: colours (hex, named, rgb, hsl, color-mix, currentcolor), linear and radial gradients, background: glass with glass-*, transform, filter, mask-image, box-shadow, border-radius, corner-shape, opacity, visibility, and borders and outlines (width, style and colour in any order, per-side colours). The border and per-side shorthands, border-style and thin, medium and thick widths are layout, in layout_writes, and share one grammar with the colour half (css/border.rs). A value it cannot read is an error with its reason; the rest of its rule still applies.\n\nHosting: Styles::set_paint_output turns on reading paint at restyle, off by default so a host that draws from resolved declarations is untouched; take_paint hands over each node's writes, with unsets for what it lost; repaint writes a node's paint again. currentcolor and em follow the node's own computed colour and font size.\n\ncss/ still builds with --no-default-features --features css-cli.\n\nChecked: unit tests for each parser and its error text, restyle tests for unsets, currentcolor following the node's colour, and borders taking layout space, plus the scene suite and the default-features build. Each parser's tests were checked by mutating the parser. Not checked: a parity diff against the other SDK's Haxe readers. One known difference from them, kept on purpose: hsl() reads a bare number for saturation or lightness as a fraction, as the Haxe reader does, which differs from CSS Color 4.\n\nConsumers: blinc_ts applies the writes to its scene natively. The HashLink SDK switching to these parsers is tracked in its own repository.","files":null}]}